> This is not part of the Ingress API, and nothing prevents ingress implementations from imposing their own restrictions or config.

@thockin, that makes sense and was my assumptionas well. However, the nginx-ingress-controller folks sent us to sig/network as they interpret the Ingress API specification to disallow their controller implementation to have such controller-specific config to identify ingresses based on .spec.ingressClassName. 
Indeed, statements like "_the field is a reference to an IngressClass resource that contains additional Ingress configuration, including the name of the Ingress controller_" in [Ingress concepts](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/ingress/) could be read as"the .spec,ingressControllerName MUST point to a valid IngressClass resource", thus my above ask to crispen the wording of the Ingress API spec to remove the uncertainty about this controller-specific config.

